				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Complete transport layer PascalCase migration and extend languages API\n\nReplace old snake_case transport implementations with stubs redirecting to canonical modules:\n- GrpcTransport.rs → redirects to gRPCTransport (PascalCase gRPC acronym)\n- IpcTransport.rs → redirects to IPCTransport (PascalCase IPC acronym)\n\nExtend LanguageNamespace with full vscode.languages API surface:\n- Add 22 register*Provider methods: hover, definition, references, code actions, document highlights, symbols, workspace symbols, rename, formatting (document/range/on-type), signature help, code lens, folding ranges, selection ranges, semantic tokens, inlay hints, type hierarchy, call hierarchy, linked editing, declarations, implementations, type definitions\n- Add set_language_configuration method\n- Update doc comment to clarify these communicate with Mountain via transport layer\n\nThis completes the transport layer restructuring and brings the VS Code API compatibility layer to parity with the upstream vscode.languages namespace.",
			"SHA": "c10204d83e10ec16f6e5afe06ddc20443d77c1f4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T08:12:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				73,
				12
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Migrate transport layer to PascalCase naming\n\nRename transport modules to follow PascalCase convention:\n- GrpcTransport.rs → gRPCTransport.rs\n- IPCTransport.rs → IPCTransport.rs (replaces IpcTransport.rs)\n\nUpdate all method names and struct fields from snake_case to PascalCase:\n- `new()` → `New()`, `with_config()` → `WithConfiguration()`\n- `connection_timeout` → `ConnectionTimeout`, `max_retries` → `MaximumRetries`\n- `as_grpc()` → `AsgRPC()`, `as_ipc()` → `AsIPC()`\n\nUpdate module paths in Strategy.rs, mod.rs, and throughout Grove to reference `Transport::Strategy::Transport` and the renamed modules. Update public API functions in mod.rs: `create_default_transport()` → `CreateDefaultTransport()`, etc.\n\nAlso fix README.md link from /why-webassembly to /why-wasm.\n\nThis completes the PascalCase migration for the Grove transport layer, ensuring consistency with the project's naming conventions.",
			"SHA": "5b390debab8001cace1e4060ae241aa4b68eb6bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T07:17:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Grove): Simplify README to focus on security philosophy\n\nRestructure README.md from detailed technical documentation to concise, philosophy-focused content. Key changes:\n\n- Add opening problem statement about VS Code extension sandbox limitations\n- Introduce zero-trust security model quote (\"sandbox enforced by hardware, not policy\")\n- Replace detailed feature lists with outcome-focused \"What It Does\" section highlighting capability-based isolation, WASM sandbox, zero-trust marketplace, and Rhai scripting\n- Update badge icons from simpleicons.org CDN to editor.land CDN\n- Condense ecosystem section to simplified Mermaid diagram\n- Remove technical sections: Building, Usage, Modules, Deep Dive, Security, Performance\n- Streamline See Also links to point to editor.land domain\n\nThe README now emphasizes the security value proposition over implementation details, targeting users who care about the \"why\" rather than the \"how\".",
			"SHA": "e72eee47bb19fe1f76349458c07d14fb990053dd"
